g and training AI models.\\n    *   The platform is used to generate synthetic data for training AI models.\\n*   **Text Data**\\n    *   Text data refers to the written information used to train AI models.\\n    *   This data can include text from various sources, such as books, articles, and websites.\\n    *   The text data is used to train language models and improve their understanding of human language.\\n*   **Video Data**\\n    *   Video data refers to the visual information used to train AI models.\\n    *   This data can include videos from various sources, such as cameras, drones, and surveillance systems.\\n    *   The video data is used to train computer vision models and improve their ability to understand and interpret visual information.\\n*   **Real Robot Data**\\n    *   Real robot data refers to the data collected from real-world robots and their interactions with their environment.\\n    *   This data can include sensor readings, images, and other types of data collected by the robot.\\n    *   The real robot data is used to fine-tune AI models and improve their performance in real-world scenarios.\\n*   **NVIDIA OSMO**\\n    *   NVIDIA OSMO is a software framework that enables the integration of multiple AI models and data sources.\\n    *   It provides a unified interface for accessing and processing different types of data.\\n    *   OSMO is used to combine the text, video, and real robot data into a single, cohesive dataset.\\n*   **Heterogeneous Compute**\\n    *   Heterogeneous compute refers to the use of different types of computing resources, such as CPUs, GPUs, and TPUs, to perform complex computations.\\n    *   This approach allows for more efficient processing of large datasets and complex AI models.\\n    *   Heterogeneous compute is used to accelerate the training and inference of AI models.\\n*   **NVIDIA Project GROOT**\\n    *   NVIDIA Project GROOT is a research project focused on developing AI models for humanoid robots.\\n    *   The project aims to create AI models that can learn from human behavior and interact with humans in a more natural way.",\n    "similarity score": 0.595512866973877\n  },\n  {\n    "6418": "6418",\n    "text": "frames/frame_6424 seconds: The image presents a flowchart illustrating the development of a humanoid robot, with a central diagram surrounded by three inset images and a robotic figure on the left side.\\n\\n*   The flowchart is divided into three main sections:\\n    *   **GROOT FOUNDATION MODEL**: This section is labeled \\"DGX\\" and is connected to the next step in the process.\\n    *   **ISAAC LAB IN OMNIVERSE**: This section is labeled \\"OVX\\" and is linked to the previous and subsequent steps.\\n    *   **GROOT STACK**: This section is labeled \\"AGX\\" and is connected to the preceding step.\\n*   The three inset images provide additional information about the robot\'s development:\\n    *   **Top-right inset**: A diagram showing the robot\'s language processing capabilities, including videos, demonstrations, observations, actions, and humanoid robots.\\n    *   **Middle-right inset**: An image of a robot navigating a complex terrain, with a gray-scale color scheme and a white sky.\\n    *   **Bottom-right inset**: A picture of a Jetson Thor robotic computer and stack, with a black background and white text.\\n*   The robotic figure on the left side of the image is depicted in a dark gray color with green accents, showcasing its mechanical design.\\n*   The background of the image is black, with a purple banner at the bottom featuring the text \\"y! highlights\\" in white letters.\\n*   The date \\"MARCH 18, 2024\\" is displayed in the top-right corner of the image.\\n\\nIn summary, the image provides a comprehensive overview of the development process for a humanoid robot, highlighting key components such as the GROOT foundation model, Isaac Lab in Omniverse, and GROOT stack. The accompanying images and diagrams offer further insight into the